+# Implementation Plan: JSON Patch (RFC 6902)
+
+**Spec**: `specs/002-json-patch/spec.md`
+
+## Technical Context
+TypeScript, no runtime deps, tests with `node --test` in `test/`. Constitution is an unfilled template: no extra gates.
+
+## Design
+- Add `applyPatch` to `src/index.ts`, reusing `parsePointer`.
+- Work on a deep clone of the document (`structuredClone`-free JSON clone helper that uses own-property definition so `__proto__` keys are safe); operations mutate the clone, so a failure discards it (atomic) and the input is untouched.
+- Values from patch (`add`/`replace`) and `copy` sources are deep-cloned on insertion.
+- Helpers: `getParent(root, tokens)` walks existing containers; `addAt`, `removeAt`, `getAt`; array index validation (canonical digits; `-` only for add).
+- Whole-document ops (`""` path) return the new root.
+- `move`: validate `from` exists; if `from === path` no-op; if `path` starts with `from + "/"` (token-prefix) throw; remove then add.
+- `test`: JSON deep equality helper.
+- Object members set via `Object.defineProperty` to be safe for `__proto__`.
+
+## Tests
+`test/patch.test.ts`: RFC 6902 appendix A examples, per-op cases, error cases, non-mutation.
